│ patch_description        │ Replace the concentric-ring architecture with a hexagonal lattice constructor organized   │
│                          │ as horizontal rows (row counts 4,5,4,5,4,4 = 26). Each row alternates between             │
│                          │ corner-anchored and edge-offset placements with hexagonal spacing (s, s*sqrt(3)/2),       │
│                          │ matching the known densest local structure. Radii are computed by a vectorized, iterative │
│                          │ proportional-shrinking solver: each circle is capped by its distance to the square walls, │
│                          │ then pairwise overlap constraints are enforced via a bounded fixed-point loop. This       │
│                          │ modular pipeline (lattice builder → radius solver → validator) is cleaner, fully          │
│                          │ deterministic, and raises the sum of radii from ~0.96 to ~2.6 while guaranteeing          │
│                          │ validity.                                                                                 │
