│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hex_lattice_layout_26                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the poor concentric-ring layout (sum ≈ 0.96) with a hexagonal (staggered-row)     │
│                          │ lattice packing of 26 equal circles. Densest local structure for equal circles is         │
│                          │ hexagonal, so rows alternate between 5 circles (unstaggered) and 4 circles (staggered by  │
│                          │ half the horizontal spacing), giving counts 5+4+5+4+5+3 = 26. With horizontal spacing s   │
│                          │ and row spacing h = s*sqrt(3)/2, the binding constraints are width 5s ≤ 1 and height s +  │
│                          │ 5h ≤ 1, i.e. s ≤ 1/(1 + 5√3/2) ≈ 0.1876, yielding uniform radius r = s/2 ≈ 0.0938 and sum │
│                          │ ≈ 2.44. The radius computation is also fixed: instead of the flawed sequential pairwise   │
│                          │ scaling, the radius is the minimum of each center's border distance and half the minimum  │
│                          │ pairwise distance (a correct uniform-radius computation for a lattice).                   │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
