│ patch_name               │ hex_grid_iterative_radius_solver                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the naive ring layout (which yields sum ≈ 0.96) with a hexagonal lattice          │
│                          │ arrangement of 26 circles — the near-optimal local structure for circle packing (density  │
│                          │ π/√12). Rows of 5,4,5,4,5,3 circles with horizontal spacing s and vertical spacing s·√3/2 │
│                          │ use the square efficiently. Then replace the one-pass radius heuristic with an iterative  │
│                          │ relaxation solver: initialize each radius to its full distance to the nearest wall, then  │
│                          │ repeatedly rescale any overlapping pair proportionally and re-clip to the walls until     │
│                          │ convergence. This is a projection onto the feasible region (non-overlap + containment)    │
│                          │ and typically converges to radii near the equal-radius hexagonal optimum (r ≈ s/2),       │
│                          │ giving a sum of radii around 2.5–2.6, close to the AlphaEvolve target of 2.635.           │
