│ patch_name               │ multi_seed_starts_best_of                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current single staggered-grid seed can get stuck in a mediocre local optimum. Known   │
│                          │ good packings of 26 circles mix hexagonal rows with corner-filling circles and unequal    │
│                          │ radii. I add several diverse seed layouts (staggered grids with different row counts, a   │
│                          │ hexagonal lattice with boundary circles, a polar/ring arrangement) and run the existing   │
│                          │ refinement + LP radius solve on each, keeping the best arrangement. This multi-start      │
│                          │ strategy substantially raises the achievable sum of radii while staying fast (few hundred │
│                          │ ms per seed), and the exact LP guarantees the reported radii remain valid for the chosen  │
│                          │ centers.                                                                                  │
