│ patch_name               │ grow_and_relax_refinement                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current uniform-radius hex lattice caps every circle at the same radius (r≈0.0938,    │
│                          │ sum 2.44). Two improvements: (1) start from a staggered-row layout (rows 5,4,5,4,5,3)     │
│                          │ with wider spacing so some circles (edges of 4-circle rows, the 3-circle row) have room   │
│                          │ to grow beyond the uniform cap; (2) replace the uniform radius computation with a         │
│                          │ per-circle Gauss-Seidel "water-filling" radius growth (each circle grows up to its border │
│                          │ distance minus neighbors' current radii), interleaved with a deterministic                │
│                          │ constraint-relaxation loop that nudges each center away from its active constraints       │
│                          │ (overlapping neighbors and walls). This mimics the structure of good non-uniform packings │
│                          │ — smaller circles at corners/edges, larger circles in roomy spots — while remaining fully │
│                          │ deterministic and guaranteeing a valid final configuration via a monotone                 │
│                          │ (radii-only-shrinking) feasibility repair pass.                                           │
