│ patch_name               │ grow_radii_relaxation                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The current layout uses 5 staggered rows (6,5,6,5,6 with the top row truncated to 4), so  │
│                          │ the arrangement doesn't fill the square vertically — the rows only span about 0.744 of    │
│                          │ the unit height. Two improvements: (1) center the rows vertically so wall distances are   │
│                          │ larger and more balanced; (2) replace the overly conservative "half nearest-neighbor      │
│                          │ distance" radius rule with an iterative fixed-point relaxation: start each radius at its  │
│                          │ full wall distance (allowing circles to grow where there is free space, e.g. the          │
│                          │ truncated top row and near walls), then repeatedly cap r_i = min(wall_i, min_j (d_ij -    │
│                          │ r_j)). This converges to a maximal valid packing where each circle is as large as         │
│                          │ possible given its neighbors, exploiting the extra space left by the two removed circles  │
│                          │ and the vertical margins, which should push the sum of radii well above the current 2.17. │
