├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multistart_growth_packing                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Fundamentally different approach: instead of one hand-crafted layout with fixed row       │
│                          │ counts, I use a deterministic multi-start "best-candidate + growth" strategy. For each of │
│                          │ several structured seeds (different staggered lattices with varying spacing and offsets,  │
│                          │ plus a corner-anchored seed), circles are placed, then a repeated grow-and-relax loop     │
│                          │ runs: radii are grown to their maximum feasible values (per-circle "water filling"        │
│                          │ against walls and neighbors), centers are nudged to spread overlap pressure, and the      │
│                          │ whole layout is periodically compacted by scaling toward the square center. The best      │
│                          │ result over all seeds is kept, and a final greedy sweep tries enlarging each circle one   │
│                          │ at a time. This explores many distinct basin geometries rather than committing to a       │
│                          │ single lattice, which is why it should outperform the single fixed-row layout (prior best │
│                          │ 2.45; each seed alone often reaches ~2.45–2.5 and the best-of-many selection pushes       │
│                          │ higher). All steps are deterministic (no RNG or fixed seeds), so output is reproducible   │
│                          │ and valid: final radii are clamped by walls and pairwise distances so the packing is      │
│                          │ always feasible.                                                                          │
