│ patch_description        │ The best prior program (score 0.93, sum 2.44) combined an LP-based optimal radius solver  │
│                          │ with a stochastic hill-climb over circle centers. The current program has the LP but      │
│                          │ lacks the center-position optimization, capping it at 2.00. I add a hill-climbing stage   │
│                          │ after the initial LP solve: iteratively jitter the centers (with directed wall-avoidance  │
│                          │ moves for wall-limited circles) and re-solve the LP, keeping improvements. This directly  │
│                          │ exploits the fact that the LP gives the exact best radii for any candidate center set, so │
│                          │ the search only optimizes the one thing the LP cannot — center positions. Expected        │
│                          │ result: match or exceed the 2.44 prior best within a modest time budget.                  │
