│ patch_description        │ The multi-start version (2.28) actually regressed below the best deterministic            │
│                          │ staggered-lattice program (2.45), and it is ~9x slower. The best-performing pattern is a  │
│                          │ single staggered hex-like seed [5,4,5,4,5,3] with wide spacing, refined by the grow/relax │
│                          │ loop with the water-filling radius solver. I propose reverting to that single             │
│                          │ deterministic seed (dropping the costly multi-start), and then adding the recommended     │
│                          │ final greedy local-search pass: after refinement, try small center shifts for each circle │
│                          │ (±δ in x and y, with shrinking δ), re-solving radii each time and keeping any shift that  │
│                          │ increases the total. This directly targets irregular center placement headroom while the  │
│                          │ monotone repair in compute_max_radii guarantees feasibility, and removing the multi-start │
│                          │ makes the search affordable within the time budget.                                       │
