│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ corner_aware_lattice_with_hill_climb                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current best program (score 0.93, sum 2.44) used an LP-based radius solver plus a     │
│                          │ hill-climb over centers, starting from a suboptimal 5/4/5/4/5/3 lattice. The current      │
│                          │ program has a better initial lattice (6/5/6/5/6 with a growth hole) but no center         │
│                          │ optimization, capping it at 2.00. I propose combining both strengths: keep the denser     │
│                          │ lattice as the starting layout, solve radii exactly with the LP at every step, and add a  │
│                          │ hill-climb over center positions. Crucially, per the corner-aware recommendation, I add   │
│                          │ directed moves that push circles touching two walls (corner circles) diagonally toward    │
│                          │ the nearest corner, where three-sided wall slack lets the LP assign them larger radii,    │
│                          │ and push single-wall circles away from walls. Small interior circles get larger jitter    │
│                          │ since they have more freedom. This should recover the ~2.44+ regime and improve on it via │
│                          │ the denser seed.                                                                          │
