│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_perturb_and_resolve                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Keep the hex seed layout and the radii solver, but wrap them in a perturb-and-resolve     │
│                          │ loop: after computing radii, measure each circle's "slack" (how much room it has to its   │
│                          │ nearest neighbor/wall constraints). Circles that are tightly constrained (little slack)   │
│                          │ are the bottleneck for the LP-like sum; iteratively push centers of tight circles away    │
│                          │ from their tightest neighbor/wall by a small step proportional to the tightness, then     │
│                          │ re-solve radii. Track the best (highest-sum) feasible configuration across iterations.    │
│                          │ This directly targets the center-placement headroom identified in prior feedback, while   │
│                          │ reusing the proven radius solver. Also add a small jitter-restart across a few relaxation │
│                          │ rounds so the search does not depend on a single trajectory.                              │
