│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ corner_aware_layout_and_multistart                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current hexagonal rows 5-4-5-4-5-3 leave corner slack: the end circles of each row    │
│                          │ sit against the side walls but the top/bottom rows only touch two walls, and the four     │
│                          │ corner regions of the square are underused. Two targeted improvements:                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Corner-aware initial placement**: shift the first/last circles of the top and bottom │
│                          │ rows diagonally into the corners (x near r, y near r, etc.), so those four circles can    │
│                          │ touch two walls simultaneously. The LP solver will then naturally assign them larger      │
│                          │ radii since the wall constraints bind in both directions. Also try squeezing the 3-circle │
│                          │ last row against the bottom wall.                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Multi-start hill-climbing**: instead of a single random-seed search, try several     │
│                          │ perturbed initial layouts (different row staggers and corner offsets) and keep the global │
│                          │ best. This diversifies basins at modest extra cost (LP with HiGHS is fast).               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. Increase iterations slightly and shrink jitter faster late in the search to fine-tune  │
│                          │ the best packing found. This pushes the sum of radii from ~2.44 toward the AlphaEvolve    │
│                          │ target of 2.635.                                                                          │
