                        Patch Metadata - Gen 22/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ greedy_growth_pass_after_hillclimb                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ After the hill-climb converges, add a deterministic greedy "growth pass": for each        │
│                          │ circle, try small shifts of its center (±step in x, y, and diagonals), re-solve the LP,   │
│                          │ and accept any shift that increases the total sum. This cheap local search directly       │
│                          │ exploits the fact that the LP solves radii exactly for fixed centers, so any center       │
│                          │ improvement translates monotonically into score. Using a small step (0.01 down to 0.002)  │
│                          │ and iterating a few times converges quickly while keeping the same runtime budget (~400   │
│                          │ LP solves × 8 directions). Combined with the recommendation header, this targets the      │
│                          │ headroom in irregular center placement left by random-jitter hill-climbing while          │
