│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_structured_multistart_seeds                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current single hexagonal-lattice start confines the search to one basin. Add a set of │
│                          │ four structurally diverse deterministic seeds (hex rows 5-4-5-4-5-3, hex rows             │
│                          │ 4-5-4-5-4-4, a dense 5-column square-like grid with 26 circles in 6 rows, and a           │
│                          │ corner-anchored layout with 4 large corner circles surrounding a 5-4-5-4 interior         │
│                          │ lattice). Each seed is LP-evaluated, then the hill-climb is run on the best seed(s) with  │
│                          │ a per-seed iteration budget, keeping the global best. This exploits the fact that n=26    │
│                          │ optimal packings are known to be non-lattice arrangements (the AlphaEvolve solution is    │
│                          │ irregular), so diverse geometric starts (especially corner-heavy ones where corner        │
│                          │ circles can grow large due to three-sided slack) give the LP-driven hill-climb access to  │
│                          │ better basins. Time budget: ~450 LP solves total (~3s at observed 0.006s per LP), well    │
│                          │ within limits.                                                                            │
