│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ spread_expansion_packing                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The prior programs plateau because symmetric pressure-relaxation cannot escape symmetric  │
│                          │ local optima. Inspired by the recommendation, I add an asymmetric "spreading" pass: each  │
│                          │ circle is pushed away from the centroid of its nearest contacts (and away from walls when │
│                          │ corner-adjacent), which inflates the packing without axis-aligned moves. I combine this   │
│                          │ with multi-restart seeds (several hex row-count patterns plus jittered variants), an      │
│                          │ over-inflation pressure loop, and exact LP radii maximization via scipy (fallback to      │
│                          │ proportional scaling). The best configuration over all restarts is returned.              │
