│ patch_name               │ hex_lp_hybrid_26pack                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the two programs: keep the LP-based hill-climb framework from the current    │
│                          │ program (which yields globally optimal radii for a given center layout), but replace the  │
│                          │ expensive scipy LP evaluation during the search loop with the fast Gauss-Seidel "water    │
│                          │ filling" + monotone repair from the second program. This makes each hill-climb iteration  │
│                          │ ~10x cheaper, letting us afford more iterations while keeping the LP only for the final,  │
│                          │ exact radius assignment. Additionally, a short deterministic overlap-repulsion refinement │
│                          │ pass (from the second program) is run first to spread clusters before random              │
│                          │ hill-climbing, and the wall-push directed moves are retained. The result should match or  │
│                          │ exceed 2.45 while cutting runtime.                                                        │
