│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ corner_anchored_seed_plus_lp                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current best result (2.47) came from a pure hexagonal lattice; the headroom toward    │
│                          │ 2.635 lies in deliberately asymmetric corner circles. Corner positions have three-sided   │
│                          │ wall slack, so the LP/water-filling solver can give them much larger radii than interior  │
│                          │ circles. I modify the seed layout to anchor 4 circles exactly in the corners (at distance │
│                          │ rc from both walls), fill the remaining 22 circles in staggered interior rows, keep the   │
│                          │ existing repulsion refinement (it will pull interior circles away from the oversized      │
│                          │ corners), and add a final exact LP solve (`solve_radii_lp`, already proven in Gen 1/2) to │
│                          │ extract the optimal unequal radii at the refined centers — the water-filling heuristic is │
│                          │ lossy, and the LP typically recovers a few percent of sum. This combines the identified   │
│                          │ corner-growth insight with the exact radii evaluation while staying fast (one LP, ~325    │
│                          │ constraints).                                                                             │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
