│ patch_description        │ Restructure around a fully vectorized NumPy solver: pairwise distances computed once as   │
│                          │ an (n,n) matrix, and radii solved by a vectorized over-relaxed Jacobi iteration (r_i =    │
│                          │ min(wall_i, min_j(d_ij − r_j)) with ω=1.5), plus a final monotone shrink repair for       │
│                          │ guaranteed feasibility. The ~10x speedup is spent on a multi-seed pipeline (several       │
│                          │ hex-lattice row patterns, corner-anchored and Halton seeds), each run through a           │
│                          │ vectorized overlap-relax refinement and a fast coordinate-descent shift search. Data      │
│                          │ flow: seeds → vectorized refine → shift search → best layout, all operating on whole      │
│                          │ arrays instead of O(n²) Python loops.                                                     │
