│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multi_seed_force_relaxation                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of a single hand-fixed hexagonal lattice followed by coordinate shifts, this      │
│                          │ approach is a population/relaxation hybrid: (1) generate many diverse structured seeds    │
│                          │ (different staggered-row counts, grids, corner-biased layouts, jittered hex lattices),    │
│                          │ (2) for each seed run a force-based relaxation — circles are given radii by the           │
│                          │ Gauss–Seidel solver, then centers are pushed apart along contact normals to release       │
│                          │ pressure on constrained circles (a physical "inflate-and-relax" scheme, fundamentally     │
│                          │ different from blind coordinate hill climbing since moves are driven by actual contact    │
│                          │ geometry), (3) the best seed after relaxation gets a final annealed coordinate descent    │
│                          │ with warm-started radius solves. This explores the configuration space much more broadly  │
│                          │ and lets contact-driven forces find anisotropic openings that single-axis shifts miss,    │
│                          │ while remaining deterministic (fixed RNG seeds) and fast.                                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
