│ patch_name               │ dual_seed_best_of_two                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Run the identical optimize pipeline (LP water-filling + corner-aware hill-climb + greedy  │
│                          │ growth pass) on two different seeds — the original wall-aligned hex lattice and the       │
│                          │ corner-anchored variant — and return the better result. This diversifies the local        │
│                          │ optimum the hill-climb lands in: the corner-anchored seed favors large corner circles     │
│                          │ with a small interior, while the wall-aligned seed spreads radius more evenly. Since the  │
│                          │ hill-climb only accepts strict LP-sum improvements, neither variant can fall below its    │
│                          │ own LP seed value, and keeping the best of the two can only help. Iterations per run are  │
│                          │ halved to keep total runtime near the previous ~9s budget.                                │
