│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ hex_rows_gs_refine_lp                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the best-performing prior script (score 0.94: hexagonal staggered-row        │
│                          │ constructor with self-consistent spacing fixed point + Gauss-Seidel water-fill radii,     │
│                          │ fast at 0.13s) with the constraint-repulsion refinement from the other programs. The new  │
│                          │ program:                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Builds the 6-row hex layout (4,5,4,5,4,4) with the fixed-point spacing so bottom/top   │
│                          │ rows touch the walls optimally.                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Applies a short deterministic repulsion refinement (moves each center away from active │
│                          │ constraints — overlapping neighbors and walls) with periodic Gauss-Seidel radius updates. │
│                          │ This improves centers without expensive LP calls per step.                                │
│                          │ 3. Computes final radii with the exact scipy LP (maximizing the sum subject to pair/wall  │
│                          │ constraints); falls back to the always-feasible Gauss-Seidel water-fill + monotone repair │
│                          │ if scipy is unavailable.                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This combines the 0.94-scoring constructor/radius solver with the center refinement that  │
│                          │ helped other variants, while avoiding the slow per-step LP hill-climb that made the       │
│                          │ current program take 10.67s.                                                              │
