│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ relocate_shift_refine_twice                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The insight summary recommends iterating the local refinement: after the first            │
│                          │ `_local_shift_search` plateaus, re-run the grow/relax refinement (`_refine`) from the     │
│                          │ improved centers, then re-enter `_local_shift_search` with only the finest deltas. The    │
│                          │ rationale is that a single pass of greedy axis-aligned shifts leaves slack: once centers  │
│                          │ move, the water-filling radii distribution changes, and coordinated multi-circle          │
│                          │ relaxations (which `_refine` provides) can unlock further small shifts that were          │
│                          │ previously rejected. This shift→relax→shift fixed-point iteration monotonically improves  │
│                          │ (we always keep the best-scoring layout) and costs little time. I also extend             │
│                          │ `_local_shift_search` with diagonal moves (both axes shifted simultaneously), since many  │
│                          │ improving directions in hexagonal layouts are neither purely horizontal nor purely        │
│                          │ vertical, and add a finer final delta (0.0005).                                           │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
