│ patch_description        │ The recommendation asks to sweep the stagger offset dx per adjacent row pair, but two     │
│                          │ prior variants also showed that corner-anchoring the seed (pulling 4 corner circles into  │
│                          │ corners) gave a large jump (2.33 → 2.40). I combine both: (a) restore corner anchoring    │
│                          │ with a small sweep of the anchor distance, and (b) sweep the stagger offsets dx ∈ {0.08,  │
│                          │ 0.09, 0.10, 0.11, 0.12} applied to staggered (5-circle) rows relative to each neighbor,   │
│                          │ running a short hill-climb + shift sweep for each candidate seed, keeping the best. This  │
│                          │ is guaranteed-not-worse: each candidate is refined independently and the best sum wins.   │
│                          │ To stay within the eval time budget, I use a cheap triage (short LP-solve + quick growth  │
│                          │ pass) for all candidates and keep the full refinement only for the best one, with reduced │
│                          │ iteration counts.                                                                         │
