│                          │ radii vector and use it as initialization for the next candidate evaluation. Since each   │
│                          │ shift moves only one circle slightly, radii converge in a handful of sweeps instead of    │
│                          │ needing full cold 300-sweep solves. This cuts the ~9s runtime dramatically, and the freed │
│                          │ budget funds more refine–shift fixed-point outer rounds (3→6), which historically each    │
│                          │ squeeze out a bit more sum (~2.49 → higher).                                              │
