│                          │ structured seed (staggered lattices, corner-anchored, Halton) gets a cheap pipeline (a    │
│                          │ short refine + one shift pass), the top-2 by solved sum advance to the full               │
│                          │ refine→shift→refine fixed point, and the final radii come from the exact scipy LP (with   │
│                          │ fast water-filling fallback + greedy enlarge). This best-of-K selection over diverse      │
│                          │ seeds is designed to escape the 2.48–2.49 lattice-basin plateau that single-seed          │
│                          │ pipelines have been stuck on, while keeping total runtime moderate since the expensive    │
